      "type": "practice",
      "subtopic": "Batch 2 · Detailed Solutions",
      "question": "If $2A3 + 3B4 = 5C7$ and $A + B + C = 12$, find $A$, $B$, $C$ (letter puzzle; assume standard typo $3B4$ not $B4$).",
      "answer": "$C = 6$; $A + B = 6$ (e.g. $A=2$, $B=4$).",
      "options": [],
      "glassboxSteps": [
        {
          "rule": "Units column",
          "why": "$3+4=7$ — no carry.",
          "math": "3 + 4 = 7"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Hundreds column",
          "why": "$2+3=5$ — matches.",
          "math": "2 + 3 = 5"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Tens column",
          "why": "No carry in or out → $A+B=C$.",
          "math": "A + B = C"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Use sum condition",
          "why": "$A+B+C=12$ and $C=A+B$.",
          "math": "C + C = 12 \\Rightarrow C = 6;\\quad A + B = 6"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "With $2A3+3B4=5C7$: $C=6$, $A+B=6$. Note: original $B4$ form is impossible.",
      "linked_note_id": "CH05-sec-playing-with-numbers",
